---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="Support"
  description="Get help with simplesolat: reminders, widgets, zones, crashes, and how to get in touch."
>
  <h1>Support</h1>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>. Tell
    me your phone model, your Android version and what happened, and I'll get
    back to you.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you have a GitHub account, you can also
    <a href={SITE.issues}>open an issue on GitHub</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Common problems</h2>

  <h3>Reminders arrive late, or not at all</h3>
  <p>
    First check that notifications are allowed for simplesolat (Settings ›
    Apps › simplesolat › Notifications).
  </p>
  <p>
    Many Android phones also stop apps running in the background to save
    battery, which delays reminders and widget updates. Set simplesolat's
    battery usage to <em>Unrestricted</em> (usually under Settings › Apps ›
    simplesolat › Battery), and allow <em>Alarms &amp; reminders</em> if your
    phone asks. The exact steps differ by brand;
    <a href="https://dontkillmyapp.com/">Don't kill my app!</a> has a guide for
    each one.
  </p>

  <h3>The widget isn't updating</h3>
  <p>
    It's usually the same battery setting as above. Widgets refresh in the
    background about every 15 minutes, and when a prayer time begins. To follow
    you when you travel, the app also needs location access
    <em>all the time</em>, not only while it's open.
  </p>

  <h3>It shows the wrong zone</h3>
  <p>
    Check that location is turned on and allowed for simplesolat. The zone is
    worked out from your location, so a rough or old location can land you in a
    neighbouring zone. Opening the app updates it.
  </p>

  <h3>The app closes as soon as I open it</h3>
  <p>
    Update simplesolat from
    <a href={SITE.playStore}>Google Play</a> first. Version 1.1.2 fixes a crash
    when opening the app.
  </p>
  <p>
    If it still closes, clear the app's data: Settings › Apps › simplesolat ›
    Storage › <em>Clear data</em>. You won't lose anything important; the app
    finds your zone again and downloads the times. If that doesn't help,
    email me.
  </p>

  <h3>The times are slightly different from my mosque</h3>
  <p>
    Where there's an official timetable, the app uses it exactly. Local mosques
    sometimes adjust by a minute or two. Outside those nine countries, times are
    calculated, and can differ a little from local practice. See
    <a href="/#sources">where the times come from</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Does simplesolat collect my data?</h3>
  <p>
    No. There's no account, no ads and no analytics, and your location never
    leaves your phone. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
